# Case of the Filched Falcon with five artifacts (four Moxen and its Clue) is solved at the turn-1 end step. "Solved - {2}{U}, Sacrifice this Case: Put four +1/+1 counters on target
# noncreature artifact. It becomes a 0/0 Bird creature with flying in addition to its other types." On Bot2's turn 2 only Moxen without blue are untapped (Mox Sapphire paid for the Case),
# so the ability is refused for mana (the {U} is short). On turn 3 it is paid exactly with Sapphire, Jet and Pearl (Mox Ruby stays untapped, the pool is empty) and sacrifices the
# Case; its own Clue becomes a Bird artifact creature with four +1/+1 counters, base 0/0 and flying: 4/4, still a Clue (its own sacrifice ability still works), and it is
# not a creature before. A noncreature artifact only: Bot1's own Clue is a legal target.

